{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review round 1 (BLOCK) — findings addressed (narration moved here to fit the 8000-char plan cap)\n\nRound-1 LLM plan-review (bedrock sonnet) returned BLOCK with three blocking findings; all are addressed in the revised plan. Detail kept here so the description stays within the review admission cap:\n\n**1 & 2 — G1G2, unenumerated consumers of the old `ignore_changes` contract.** Two GATING consumers assert the opcert key still declares `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }` and would regress to RED:\n- `infra/terraform/opcert-plan-assertions.sh` assertion **(f)** hard-fails (exit 1) unless `opcert.tf` declares that block on `opcert_ed25519_key`. Fix: rewrite (f) to assert the key param declares `value_wo` (+ `value_wo_version`) — the new no-clobber invariant.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` — `test_terraform_both_securestring_params_present` (line 69, key-param `ignore_changes` regex) and `test_assertion_script_present_executable_and_literal` (line 164, asserts the script contains `.lifecycle_meta_arguments.ignore_changes`). Both move to the `value_wo` invariant; the `opcert_origin_guard` guard-param assertions are unchanged.\n- Non-gating but directly-related docs refreshed: `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md` (cookie-signing row) and `infra/runbooks/gerrit-auth-hardening.md`.\n- Verified there are NO other test/script consumers asserting value/ignore on `rebar_secrets` or `cookie_signing_secret` (`grep` across `tests/`, `scripts/`, `infra/`). `test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:553` asserts on `rebar_plain_seeded` (a non-secret String param) — out of scope.\n\n**3 — G6, the CUTOVER clobber.** Correct and important: on the migration apply, `value_wo_version` transitions ABSENT→1, which the AWS provider treats as a change and re-sends `value_wo = \"CHANGEME\"`, RESETTING each already-seeded live secret to the placeholder on that single apply. Steady-state no-clobber still holds (value re-sent only on a later `value_wo_version` bump). Reconciliation: this reset is acceptable and INTENDED because the same exposure mandates ROTATING these secrets anyway — the deferred operator ticket runs the apply and the re-seed/rotation in ONE maintenance window (apply → all affected slots are `CHANGEME` → operator seeds the NEW rotated value into each via `aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite`), with `user_data.sh`'s `CHANGEME` fail-fast as the safety net and a back-out note in the runbook. The code change runs no apply.\n\n**RED→GREEN oracle result (prototyped hermetically against copies of the three .tf files):** the guard is RED on the current tree with exactly 6 findings (the 3 seeded-secret resources × {literal-value, ignore_changes}); `opcert_origin_guard` (generated value) and the `String` params are correctly NOT flagged; GREEN (exit 0) after the value_wo migration; and reverting one param to `value + ignore_changes` returns it to RED (mutation teeth)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788024364895601653,"uuid":"080c8fad-c8ef-45ed-b789-ae38ec5e61c5"}